# Build-context exclusions shared by all images in deploy/.
#
# Purpose: keep `docker build` contexts small — the Rust builder only needs
# Cargo manifests + crates/, the web builder only needs the pnpm workspace.
# The two code-graph caches at the end are gitignored agent output that no
# image reads; they were 103 MB (.trail) plus 88 MB (graphify-out) of context
# sent to the daemon on every build before they were listed here.
.git
.kilo
.github
target
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
coverage
design
docs
scripts
.trail
graphify-out
# Trees no image in deploy/ reads (verified against the COPY lists in
# Dockerfile.rust and Dockerfile.web). Both images only need: crates, plugins,
# desktop, installer, .sqlx, packages/{sdk,ui,layout}, apps/web, LEGAL/fonts and
# deploy/*.cjs. Keeping these out shrinks the context sent to the daemon on
# every build. deploy/backup, deploy/edge and deploy/postgres stay: other
# Dockerfiles COPY from them.
e2e
fixtures
native
website
apps/installer
release-keys
deploy/helm
deploy/observability
deploy/runbooks
